5,Apal - accentnetwork.com,https://accentnetwork.com/apal/,"Apr 22, 2025 · Apal’s phonetics are characterized by a relatively small set of sounds, with emphasis on consonants. It might pose pronunciation challenges for non-native speakers due to unique consonant combinations.",Apal,Trans-New Guinea
6,Top 10 Papua New Guinean Musicians Recognized Internationally,https://journeywitin.wordpress.com/2025/01/29/top-10-papua-new-guinean-musicians-recognized-worldwide/,"Jan 29, 2025 · In this post, we highlight ten artists whose music has made an impact beyond the shores of PNG. 1. George Telek is one of PNG’s most internationally acclaimed musicians. His unique fusion of traditional Tolai sounds with contemporary influences has captivated global audiences.",Apal,Trans-New Guinea
7,database of the languages of New Guinea,https://transnewguinea.org/language/apali,"Classification: Nuclear Trans New Guinea, Madang, Kalamic-South Adelbert, South Adelbert, Sogeram, Apalic.",Apal,Trans-New Guinea
8,Apal / Apali,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Apal.htm,"Other comments: Apali or Apal is spoken by approximately 900 speakers in Aiome district, upper Ramu river area, Madang province, Papua New Guinea. The Apali language has a digit-tally system up to twenty in traditional way.",Apal,Trans-New Guinea
